    "created_at": "2025-02-06T03:03:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-06T03:03:17Z",
    "body": "I think this is merely editorial. Do you agree?\n\nMy logic is that _key_ only ever is same-origin with _origin_ when:\n- _origin_ is an opaque origin, or\n- step 3 is executed, which sets _key_ = origin_, or\n- step 5.1 is executed, which sets _key_ = _origin_, or\n- step 4 is executed, in which case step 6.3 will not be.\n\nSo within this algorithm, _key_ is same-origin with _origin_ iff _key_ equals _origin_.\n\nThis is subtle and so probably we should fix it to be clearer. But I want to double-check there is no case I'm missing where the difference actually matters.",
