    "updated_at": "2025-02-06T12:26:27Z",
    "body": "That's true. We'll never reach 6.3 with _key_ = _origin_ unless it's the actual invocation of obtain-similar-origin-window where we set _key_ to exactly _origin_.\n\nSo I guess it's a matter of comparing site (2-tuple) to an origin (either opaque or 4-tuple) when _key_ is _site_. They're obviously different, so maybe it's actually fine.\n\nYeah, definitely editorial I think after thinking it through again.\n\n@zcorpan did we talk about anything else that I've forgotten?",
